1. Definitions
--------------

1.1. "Contributor"
    means each individual or entity that creates, contributes to the
    creation of, or owns Existing Code or Modifications.

1.2. "Contributor Version"
    means the combination of the Original Software, prior Modifications,
    and the Modifications made by that particular Contributor.

1.3. "Covered Software"
    means the Source Code Form to which the initial Contributor has attached
    the notice in Exhibit A, the Executable Form of such Source Code Form, and
    Modifications of such Source Code Form, in each case including portions
    thereof.

1.4. "Executable Form"
    means any form for which the Source Code Form has been compiled,
    transformed, or translated, including object code, assembly code,
    bytecode, and binary forms.

1.5. "Initial Contributor"
    means the individual or entity that distributes the Covered Software
    under this License.

1.6. "Larger Work"
    means a work that combines Covered Software with other material, in
    a separate file or files, that is not Covered Software.

1.7. "Licensable"
    means having the right to grant, to the maximum extent possible,
    whether at the time of the initial grant or subsequently, any and all
    of the rights granted herein.

1.8. "Modifications"
    means any of the following:

    a. any file in Source Code Form that results from an addition to,
       deletion from, or modification of the contents of Covered Software;
       or

    b. any new file in Source Code Form that contains any Covered
       Software.

1.9. "Original Software"
    means Covered Software that is not a Modification.

1.10. "Source Code Form"
    means the ordinary form of Covered Software for making modifications.

1.11. "You" (or "Your")
    means an individual or a legal entity exercising rights under this
    License. For legal entities, "You" includes any entity that
    controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with You. For
    purposes of this definition, "control" means (a) the power, direct or
    indirect, to cause the direction or management of such entity,
    whether by contract or otherwise, or (b) ownership of more than
    fifty percent (50%) of the outstanding shares or beneficial
    ownership of such entity.

